course: dictionary
lesson: 2997
title: Dunes: hills of sand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dune is a hill or ridge of sand that the wind has piled up. You will find dunes in deserts and near the sea. Wind keeps moving the sand, so dunes slowly change shape.
explain: Context helps you work out the meaning. «She keeps her hole shallow and does not dig a tunnel under the dune.» Digging a hole and a tunnel means the dune is something you can dig into, so it must be a pile of sand.
explain: On beach trips, dunes protect the land from the sea, so we stay on the marked paths. You may meet the phrases «sand dune», «sand dunes» and «behind the dunes». Each one means the same kind of sandy hill.
fact: A dune is a hill or ridge of sand.
fact: Wind piles the sand up into dunes, and it moves them slowly.
fact: «Dune» means a hill or ridge of sand piled up by the wind, in a desert or near the sea.
fact: «Most of the world's deserts are rock, gravel, mountains or ice; only about a fifth to a quarter of the Sahara is sand dunes.»
fact: The fog-basking beetle of the Namib Desert stands on a dune at dawn, and engineers have copied its bumpy back to collect water from fog.
exercise: In geography lessons, what usually makes a dune? | Water pouring down a river | Rocks rolling down a cliff | *Wind piling up sand | Snow falling on a mountain
exercise: «Most of the world's deserts are rock, gravel, mountains or ice.» What does this tell you? | Dunes are found only in cities | All deserts are covered in sand dunes | *Most deserts are not mainly sand dunes | The Sahara has no sand at all
exercise: Where can you usually find dunes? | Only on the tops of mountains | On the Moon | Inside a cave | *In a desert or near the sea
test: «The fog-basking beetle stands head-down on a dune at dawn.» What is a dune in this sentence? | A kind of fish | A type of tree | A cloud of fog | *A hill of sand
test: Why do sand dunes slowly change shape? | Because they are made of rock | *Because the wind keeps moving the sand | Because people paint them | Because it rains every day
exam: «A sand dune collapsed on them, probably burying them in a moment.» What probably buried the fossil animals? | A landslide of rock | A volcano erupting | A flood of water | *A sand dune collapsing
